import support.dl
import ../src/enforcer.dl

create a temporary directory
set temporary to it
expect truth temporary succeeded
set root to temporary's directory path
set source_path to repository path from root and "sample.rs"
set source to the string form of "pub fn BadFunction() {}\n"
write source to the file at source_path
expect truth it succeeded

set loaded to load conventions from "naming:\n  repository:\n    case: kebab-case\n  directory:\n    case: snake_case\n  language:\n    rust:\n      function: snake_case\n      file: snake_case\n"
expect truth loaded's succeeded
set arguments to an empty list of string
set backend to a language backend named "rust" using "rust-analyzer" with arguments
set backends to a list containing backend
set enforced to enforce conventions in working copy root for repository "demo" using loaded's conventions and backends with git "git", applying fixes true
expect falsehood enforced's succeeded
expect falsehood enforced's changed
expect enforced's error message to equal "Rust convention enforcement requires a root Cargo.toml workspace manifest"
expect the length of enforced's report's failures to equal 1
read the file at source_path and set unchanged to it
expect truth unchanged succeeded
expect unchanged's contents to equal source

free convention enforcement result enforced
free backends
free language backend backend
free conventions result loaded
remove the filesystem tree at root
expect truth it succeeded

print "rust manifest: passed" as a line
